    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n15908" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀρχ-ιᾱτρός</span></b>  (on the accent v. Hdn.Gr.<i><span class="en">
			1.229
		</span></i>), 
			Ion.
		
		<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀρχ-ιητρός</span></b> , ὁ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>court</i> or
				<i>official physician</i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>OGI</u>
				256.5
			</span></i> (Delos, <span class="entity">ii/i B.C.</span>), etc.; of the Roman
			Emperors, <i><span class="en">
				Gal.
				14.2
			</span></i>, al.; of communities, <i>arch. populares</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Cod.Theod.
				13.3
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Cod.Just.</u>
				10.52.10
			</span></i>, al.: generally, <i>responsible practitioner,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Aret.
				<u>CA</u>
				2.5
			</span></i>; cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀρχιίατρος.</span></div>
